# Build-context hygiene for `context: ./backend` (docker-compose.yml:32-34).  There was NO
# .dockerignore anywhere in this repo, so the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` (backend/Dockerfile:20) shipped
# the whole directory into every image layer — gitignored runtime state included.

# SECURITY-CRITICAL: `data/` is the parent of the DeepSeek key store
# (`DEEPSEEK_KEY_FILE` default `data/deepseek_api_key.json` — the path the Settings page writes).
# Without this line, a build on a host where a key was saved bakes the secret into an image layer
# (which survives `docker save` and a registry push) while the `backend_data:/app/data` volume makes
# it invisible at runtime.  The volume supplies /app/data at runtime; nothing in the image is built
# from the build host's data/.
data/

# Dev/runtime state and caches: the container installs its own dependencies and the Dockerfile only
# pip-installs requirements.txt, so none of this is an input to the image.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
junit.xml
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Secrets are never build inputs (a copied env file persists in the layer; use secret mounts if a
# build ever genuinely needs one).
.env
.env.*

# The image never runs pytest — the Makefile's test targets use the host venv and no compose service
# mounts the repo — so the suite has no business in the layer.
tests/
